/-!
# Bilinear Marcinkiewicz interpolation

This file was automatically generated by Claude.

We prove a form of the multilinear Marcinkiewicz interpolation theorem for bilinear operators
with a quasi-Banach target (`bilinear_marcinkiewicz`).

Let `T` be a bilinear operator from pairs of simple functions (with finite measure support) on
`(X, μ)` and `(Y, ν)` to measurable functions on `(Z, ρ)`. Write `s = 1/p`, `t = 1/q` for the
target reciprocal exponents and `1/r = s + t`. Suppose that for some `0 < δ < min s t` the
operator satisfies weak-type bounds at the four corners `(s ± δ, t ± δ)`:
`‖T f g‖_{L^{r_c,∞}} ≤ A ‖f‖_{p_c} ‖g‖_{q_c}` with `1/p_c = s ± δ`, `1/q_c = t ± δ` and
`1/r_c = 1/p_c + 1/q_c`. Then `T` satisfies the strong bound
`‖T f g‖_{L^r} ≤ C ‖f‖_p ‖g‖_q`. The exponent `r` may be smaller than `1`, and no restriction
`s, t < 1` is needed. The weak quasinorm is `weakLpNorm ρ r v = sup_{τ > 0} τ ρ{|v| > τ}^{1/r}`.

## Proof idea

By homogeneity we may assume `‖f‖_p = ‖g‖_q = 1`. For every height `λ > 0` we split
`f = f₁ + f₂` with `f₁ = f 1{|f| ≥ λ^{r/p}}` and similarly `g = g₁ + g₂` at height `λ^{r/q}`
(`piece`). Then `ρ{|T f g| > λ} ≤ ∑_{a,b} ρ{|T f_a g_b| > λ/4}`, and each of the four terms is
estimated by the weak bound at the corner whose exponents lie on the favourable side of
`(p, q)` (`p_c < p` for the large part, `p_c > p` for the small part). Inserting the
layer-cake formula `∫ |T f g|^r = r ∫_0^∞ λ^{r-1} ρ{|T f g| > λ} dλ`, the product
`‖f_a‖_{p_c}^{r_c} ‖g_b‖_{q_c}^{r_c}` is split by the elementary inequality
`P^u Q^v ≤ P + Q` (`u + v = 1`, a crude form of Hölder's inequality in `λ`), and Tonelli's
theorem (for simple functions just an interchange of a finite sum and an integral) reduces
everything to the one-dimensional integrals `∫_0^{M} λ^α dλ` and `∫_M^∞ λ^α dλ`, which
reproduce `∫ |f|^p` and `∫ |g|^q`.
